ion Hematology Topics-in-Focus program\nHemoglobinopathies Topics-in-Focus program\nCongress\nHemaSphere\nAbout EHA\nSearch\nJoin EHA\nLogin\nEmpowering progress, knowledge, and partnership.\nWelcome to Borderless Hematology.\nEHA is the leading force in hematology, bringing the community together to share knowledge, collaborate, connect, and grow.\nTogether we accelerate progress through education, science, and innovation. Together we improve patient outcomes and progress towards cures—across Europe and beyond.\nTogether, the future of hematology is within our reach.\nJoin us with membership that works for you or learn more about our story.\nEHA2027 Congress\nEuropean affairs\nEHA Campus\nGrants\nSpecialized Working Groups\nWhat’s new?\nGo to overview\nTuesday, September 29, 2026\nEHA's Long-Term Advocacy for Hematology Achieves a Major Milestone\nTuesday, September 22, 2026\nInterview with EHA’s European Affairs Committee Member, Ariane Weinman\nThursday, July 23, 2026\nASCERTAIN project for better pricing and reimbursement models enters final phase\nWednesday, July 22, 2026\nInterview with EHA’s European Affairs Committee Member, Kate Morgan\nMonday, July 6, 2026\nPublication of EHA Annual General Meeting 2026 minutes\nReady to join our community?\nOur network is not just a professional association; it’s a community that nurtures growth, membership, and innovation in a manner that transcends geographical and intellectual borders. To us, this is Borderless Hematology.\nJoin EHA today\nEHA Mentorship Program\nBecome a mentor today\nMentoring is about more than sharing knowledge. It’s about building connections, gaining fresh perspectives, and helping shape the future of hematology.\nIf you believe in the power of community and want to support the next generation of hematology professionals, we’d love to welcome you as an EHA Mentor.\nBecome an EHA mentor today\nUpcoming events\nGo to overview\nEHA-SHTRM Balkan Hematology Tutorial 2026\nOctober 23–24, 2026\nChișinău, Moldova\nIn-Person\nEHA-SOCHIHEM LATAM Hematology Tutorial\nNovember 5–6, 2026\nSantiago, Chile\nIn-Person\nEHA Topics-in-Focus Preceptorship on Hemoglobinopathies: From Diagnosis and Prevention, to Personalized Management and Cure\nNovember 16–18, 2026\nAthens, Greece\nIn-Person\nEHA-EBMT 9th European CAR T-cell Meeting\nFebruary 4–6, 2027\nLisbon, Portugal\nIn-Person\nEHA-SWG Scientific Meeting on Iron and Erythropoiesis: bridging molecular mechanism and clinical practice\nSeptember 9–11, 2027\nPrague, Czechia\nIn-Person\nJoin EHA\nFull membership\nJunior membership\n60-day trial\nGet involved\nCareer development\nScientific meetings\nAbout us\nMission and vision\nJobs\nSponsor EHA\nContact us\nFollow us\nPrivacy statement\nTerms and conditions\nSubscribe\nCopyright © 2026\nBecome an EHA Mentor\nEHA Mentorship Program\nDiscover the rewards of mentoring\nApply by October 29\nApply today",
